{number: 154}
{title: Just A Closer Walk with Thee}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I am weak, but Thou art strong;
Jesus, [G7] keep me from all wrong;
I’ll be [C] satisfied as long
As I [F] walk, let me [C] walk [G7] close to [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Just a closer walk with Thee,
Grant it, [G7] Jesus, is my plea,
Daily [C] walking close to [F] Thee:
Let it [C] be, dear [G7] Lord, let it [C] be.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Through [C] this world of toil and snares,
If I [G7] falter, Lord, who cares?
Who with [C] me my burden shares?
None but [F] Thee, dear [C] Lord, [G7] none but [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
When [C] my feeble life is o’er,
Time for [G7] me will be no more;
Guide me [C] gently, safely o’er
To Thy [F] kingdom [C] shore, [G7] to Thy [C] shore.
{end_of_verse}
